":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 78 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 8.2 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 9.5, with a 95% confidence interval of 6.4 to 14.2. December accounts for 14% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 7% of all its services and supplies contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 4. Contract [1], for 14,921.43 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The data shows a pattern of contracts just under the limit, but it doesn't prove any wrongdoing. Prices could be standard, budgets fixed, or needs separate. Statistical trends don't indicate improper actions by any party.\nWhat can be checked: Check the December contracts for unusual frequency. Review awardee A's contracts to see if they repeat the same service. Look at contract [1] to see what was purchased and how it fits within the legal limit.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["PvieVYVs03mHCIsjvJ3rhQ%3D%3D","ix1N%2BP5KEimOUi78BmzhOQ%3D%3D","3h4Yuotn7l%2BAAM7L03kM8A%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}